\ ==== fill-triangle ( x0 y0 x1 y1 x2 y2 -- ), offline ====

\ fill-triangle fills, in the current ink, every pixel whose centre lies
\ inside the triangle: each row from its centre's crossings with the edges,
\ a pixel filled when its centre lies between them; clipped to the canvas.
\ Drawing needs no window, so capture-bitmap reads the canvas back.

: show-rows ( bitmap -- )
	| bitmap |
	bitmap dim to n-columns to n-rows
	0 n-rows 1 do row
		"" 0 n-columns 1 do column
			bitmap row column @i,j 0 = if "." else "#" then +
		loop . cr
	loop ;

: blank ( -- ) 0 ink 0 0 12 12 fill-rect 0xffffff ink ;

\ === a right triangle, its corners on pixel corners: row 0's centre, y 0.5, meets the long edge at x 5.5, so pixels 0 to 4 ===
blank
0 0 6 0 0 6 fill-triangle
0 0 7 7 capture-bitmap show-rows
\ #####..
\ ####...
\ ###....
\ ##.....
\ #......
\ .......
\ .......
clear

\ === the same corners in another order fill the same pixels ===
blank
0 6 6 0 0 0 fill-triangle
0 0 7 7 capture-bitmap show-rows
\ #####..
\ ####...
\ ###....
\ ##.....
\ #......
\ .......
\ .......
clear

\ === a thin sliver: row 1's centre, y 1.5, meets the upper edge at x 5.83, so pixels 0 to 5; rows 0 and 2 have their centres outside ===
blank
0 1 7 1.6 0 2 fill-triangle
0 0 7 3 capture-bitmap show-rows
\ .......
\ ######.
\ .......
clear

\ === clipped to the canvas: corners off it draw the part on it; row 0's centre meets the long edge at x 4.5 ===
blank
-5 -5 10 -5 -5 10 fill-triangle
0 0 6 6 capture-bitmap show-rows
\ ####..
\ ###...
\ ##....
\ #.....
\ ......
\ ......
clear

\ === corners in a line fill nothing ===
blank
0 0 3 3 6 6 fill-triangle
0 0 4 4 capture-bitmap show-rows
\ ....
\ ....
\ ....
\ ....
clear

\ === errors ===
0 0 1 1 2 "a" fill-triangle                                 \ (a coordinate that is not a number)
0 0 1 1 fill-triangle                                       \ (too few coordinates)
